{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "CLowl shared conformance fixture suite. Cases exercise the two hand-maintained CLASS validators (TS CLowlMessage.validate / Python CLowlMessage.validate) in BOTH strict and lenient parse modes. Consumed by both SDK runners plus fixtures/divergence_gate.py. Verdict vocab: valid | invalid | roundtrip_ok | roundtrip_mismatch.",
    "conformance_pair": "TS src/message.ts CLowlMessage.validate / fromDict / parseLenient <-> Python clowl.py CLowlMessage.validate / from_dict / parse_lenient. NOT TS schema.ts validateSchema() (TS-only, stricter, no Python analog).",
    "modes": {
      "strict": "run fromDict(input) (default) -> validate. expected_verdict is the strict verdict.",
      "lenient": "run parseLenient(input) (opt-in) -> validate. expected_lenient_verdict is the lenient verdict; when absent it defaults to expected_verdict. Cases with expected_coercions also assert the produced coercion_warnings (order-independent) in each SDK."
    },
    "classes": {
      "valid": "strict validate() -> expect valid",
      "invalid": "strict validate() (construction that would raise is caught -> invalid) -> expect invalid",
      "coercible": "invalid under strict; lenient coerces into the declared schema and graduates to valid with coercion_warnings",
      "roundtrip": "if invalid -> invalid; else compare parse->toDict() against expected_roundtrip -> roundtrip_ok | roundtrip_mismatch"
    },
    "convergence_notes": "OSA-1153 item 1 converged the latent divergences item 3 held out: wrong clowl version is now strict-invalid in BOTH SDKs (Python stopped hardcoding 0.2 on parse; both now read and validate the field); non-string tid/pid and non-boolean det are strict-invalid in BOTH (lenient stringifies/coerces); float ts is strict-invalid in BOTH (TS added an integer check to match Python); missing p/from/to/cid returns invalid in Python instead of raising KeyError (aligned with the TS no-throw path). pid:null stays valid both modes both SDKs; unknown/extra fields are ignored consistently and stay valid. Integral-float ts truncation is intentionally NOT gated: JS Number has no int/float distinction, so an integral-valued float is indistinguishable from an integer in TS. The float-ts case therefore uses a non-integral float, which both SDKs reject in strict AND lenient."
  },
